tem-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 Capture default text output and `--json` output for the five matrix inputs into the packet scratch folder (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the `--quiet, -q` convention and its exact help wording in the sibling scripts (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` in the globals block (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add a `--quiet|-q` case that sets `QUIET_OUTPUT=true` and shifts one argument, without consuming a value (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Add the quiet early return at the top of `output_text()`, printing only `Recommended Level: <level> (<name>)` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 [P] Update the file header OPTIONS block with `--quiet, -q` and the JSON composition rule (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 [P] Update `show_help()` with the same option entry and a quiet example (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 Write the regression harness: quiet one-line assertion, default first-line parity, JSON parity, error paths, help assertion, flag-order rows (`runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh`)\n- [ ] T010 Run `bash -n` on the modified script and the new harness (`recommend-level.sh`, `runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Run the harness and confirm every row passes (`runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh`)\n- [ ] T012 Diff default text output against the Phase 1 baseline for all five inputs; the diff must be empty (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/`)\n- [ ] T013 Diff `--json` output against the baseline with and without `--quiet`; both diffs must be empty (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/`)\n- [ ] T014 Confirm `--help` lists `--quiet, -q`, that `--quiet --help` still prints full help and exits `0`, and that error paths exit `1` (`recommend-level.sh`)\n- [ ] T015 Record the harness output and diff results as evidence in this packet, then run `validate.sh --strict` (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/`)\n- [ ] T016 Clean the packet scratch folder of temporary captures (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Baseline captures exist for every matrix input\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n` passes on the script and the harness\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] `shellcheck` reports no new finding