{"toolCallId":"call_e86f7024f2604967b67beea3fb4aa101","title":"Searched for \\[[A-Za-z][^]]*\\] in ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"rg -n \"\\[[A-Za-z][^]]*\\]\" specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"rg -n \"\\[[A-Za-z][^]]*\\]\" specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md | head -40","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["rg"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_e976fa3f5b6c4e9786eec88526a0b957","title":"Read file","kind":"read","locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"read"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ebe491d44c5544a99b33d9bf5c7f9f56","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Callers that only need the recommended level must capture and filter a multi-section report to recover one value. This packet specifies an additive --quiet flag that prints only the recommended-level line, while the default report and the JSON payload stay byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` always prints a full report: level, score, confidence, a\nfour-row breakdown and an optional phase section. A caller that wants only the\nlevel has to capture that report and filter it. This packet adds an opt-in\n`--quiet` / `-q` flag that prints exactly one line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`,\nand changes nothing when the flag is absent.\n\n**Key Decisions**: quiet affects the human-readable renderer only; `--json` output\nis unchanged. The flag name and short alias follow the `--quiet, -q` convention\nalready used by sibling spec scripts.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: None beyond the Bash runtime already required by the\nscript. No new packages, no configuration.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-25 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n`output_text()` prints seven to fourteen lines for a single answer. Automation\nthat needs the level, such as a hook or a shell prompt helper, has to capture the\nwhole report and parse the first line or grep for `Recommended Level:`. That\nfiltering is repeated in every caller and breaks silently if the report's leading\nblank line or section order ever changes.\n\n### Purpose\n\nGive callers a documented, stable one-line output mode so the level can be read\nwithout parsing the report, while leaving every existing invocation unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n\n- A `--quiet` flag with the `-q` short alias on `recommend-level.sh`\n- A quiet branch in the text renderer that prints only the recommended-level line\n- Header comment and `show_help()` entries for the new flag, including how it\n  composes with `--json`\n- A shell regression harness covering quiet output, default-output parity and\n  the error paths\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Changing the default report, its wording or its section order - existing\n  callers and human readers depend on it\n- Changing the JSON schema or adding a quiet-specific JSON payload - JSON is\n  already machine-readable and carries `recommended_level`\n- Changing scoring, thresholds, phase logic or exit codes - unrelated to the\n  flag and out of scope for this packet\n- Adding `--quiet` to other spec scripts - `validate.sh`,\n  `progressive-validate.sh` and `check-completion.sh` already implement it, and\n  each has its own output contract\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add `--quiet`/`-q` parsing, a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, a quiet early return in `output_text()`, and help text |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh` | Create | Regression harness for quiet output, default parity and error paths |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` and `-q` are accepted by the argument parser and set quiet mode without consuming a value. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and text output, stdout contains exactly one line: `Recommended Level: <level> (<name>)`, with no leading blank line, no score line, no breakdown and no phase section. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout and stderr are byte-identical to the pre-change script for every input in the test matrix. |\n| REQ-004 | Exit codes are unchanged: `0` on a successful recommendation, `1` on the existing usage and validation errors. Quiet mode never suppresses a stderr error message. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-005 | `--quiet` composes with the existing flags (`--loc`, `--files`, `--auth`, `--api`, `--db`, `--architectural`, `--recommend-phases`, `--no-recommend-phases`, `--phase-threshold`) in any order, and repeating it is idempotent. |\n| REQ-006 | `--quiet` combined with `--json` leaves the JSON payload unchanged; quiet is a documented no-op in JSON mode so the schema stays single and stable. |\n| REQ-007 | The script header OPTIONS block and `show_help()` both document `--quiet, -q` and the JSON composition rule. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --quiet` prints one line and exits `0`.\n- **SC-002**: A diff of default text output before and after the change is empty across all five matrix inputs.\n- **SC-003**: A diff of `--json` output before and after the change is empty across the same inputs, with and without `--quiet`.\n- **SC-004**: The regression harness passes every row and `bash -n` accepts both the script and the harness.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 compatibility (macOS system bash) | A construct such as `${var,,}` would fail on the default macOS shell | Use the script's existing `[[ \"$VAR\" = true ]]` idiom; no new Bash-4-only syntax |\n| Dependency | `set -euo pipefail` | An unset `QUIET_OUTPUT` aborts the run | Initialize the global beside `JSON_OUTPUT` before parsing; test the no-flag path first |\n| Risk | A quiet branch placed at the wrong layer changes the JSON path too | Breaking change for `speckit-plan.yaml` and `speckit-complete.yaml` callers | Guard inside `output_text()` only; `output_json()` stays untouched and is diff-tested |\n| Risk | Option parsing regresses on a value that looks like a flag | Existing `--loc --quiet` style misuse changes behavior | Keep the existing `[[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]` guards; add matrix rows for missing values |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: The flag adds one boolean branch; total runtime stays within the\n  script's current startup cost and adds no measurable latency for either mode.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The flag accepts no value and opens no new input surface. The\n  script continues to read no environment secrets and writes no files.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for identical inputs. Quiet mode emits the\n  same level and name the default report's first line emits.\n- **NFR-C01**: Default text output and JSON output are backward compatible\n  byte-for-byte; no in-repo caller needs a change.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` alone still fails the existing `At least --loc or --files`\n  validation, exits `1`, and writes the error to stderr only.\n- Maximum length: not applicable; the flag carries no value.\n- Large inputs: `--loc 2000 --files 40 --quiet` still prints one line; phase\n  scoring runs exactly as it does today.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- Missing numeric value after `--loc` or `--files`: unchanged `ERROR:` on stderr\n  and exit `1`, even when `--quiet` is also present.\n- Unknown option: unchanged `ERROR: Unknown option` on stderr and exit `1`.\n- `--quiet` repeated: idempotent, one line.\n- `--quiet --json`: JSON payload unchanged; quiet has no effect in JSON mode.\n- `--quiet --help`: help prints in full and exits `0`; help takes precedence.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 5/25 | Files: 2, LOC: ~40 including the harness, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 5/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N, public CLI surface: Y |\n| Research | 3/20 | Existing option parsing and sibling `--quiet` convention read, no investigation |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **15/100** | **Level 3 declared by the operator for this authoring packet** |\n\nThe change itself scores in Level 0 territory on the script's own algorithm. The\npacket is Level 3 because it was created with `--level 3`; the documentation\ndepth is a deliberate choice, not a complexity signal.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | Default output drifts while adding the quiet branch | H | L | Byte-diff against a captured baseline across five inputs |\n| R-002 | Quiet leaks into the JSON path and breaks command assets | H | L | Guard only in `output_text()`; JSON parity row in the harness |\n| R-003 | A new Bash-4-only construct breaks macOS system bash | M | L | Reuse the existing boolean idiom and run `bash -n` |\n| R-004 | Quiet line drifts from the default report's first line | M | M | Harness asserts equality between the two strings |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line level for automation (Priority: P0)\n\n**As an** automation author wiring `recommend-level.sh` into a hook or prompt\nhelper, **I want** a flag that prints only the level, **so that** I can read one\nvalue without parsing a report whose formatting I do not control.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-001, AC-002, AC-005).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Quiet answer for a human operator (Priority: P1)\n\n**As an** operator checking a task's level in a terminal, **I want** a concise\nanswer on demand, **so that** I can see the level without scrolling past a\nbreakdown I did not ask for.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-003, AC-007).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. The quiet-plus-JSON composition is decided in `plan.md` ADR-001, and the\n  flag naming is decided in ADR-002.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: ADR-001 and ADR-002 are recorded in `plan.md` under the\n  L3 Architecture Decision Record section; this packet does not create a separate\n  `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Callers that only need the recommended level must capture and filter a multi-section report to recover one value. This packet specifies an additive --quiet flag that prints only the recommended-level line, while the default report and the JSON payload stay byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` always prints a full report: level, score, confidence, a\nfour-row breakdown and an optional phase section. A caller that wants only the\nlevel has to capture that report and filter it. This packet adds an opt-in\n`--quiet` / `-q` flag that prints exactly one line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`,\nand changes nothing when the flag is absent.\n\n**Key Decisions**: quiet affects the human-readable renderer only; `--json` output\nis unchanged. The flag name and short alias follow the `--quiet, -q` convention\nalready used by sibling spec scripts.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: None beyond the Bash runtime already required by the\nscript. No new packages, no configuration.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-25 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n`output_text()` prints seven to fourteen lines for a single answer. Automation\nthat needs the level, such as a hook or a shell prompt helper, has to capture the\nwhole report and parse the first line or grep for `Recommended Level:`. That\nfiltering is repeated in every caller and breaks silently if the report's leading\nblank line or section order ever changes.\n\n### Purpose\n\nGive callers a documented, stable one-line output mode so the level can be read\nwithout parsing the report, while leaving every existing invocation unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n\n- A `--quiet` flag with the `-q` short alias on `recommend-level.sh`\n- A quiet branch in the text renderer that prints only the recommended-level line\n- Header comment and `show_help()` entries for the new flag, including how it\n  composes with `--json`\n- A shell regression harness covering quiet output, default-output parity and\n  the error paths\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Changing the default report, its wording or its section order - existing\n  callers and human readers depend on it\n- Changing the JSON schema or adding a quiet-specific JSON payload - JSON is\n  already machine-readable and carries `recommended_level`\n- Changing scoring, thresholds, phase logic or exit codes - unrelated to the\n  flag and out of scope for this packet\n- Adding `--quiet` to other spec scripts - `validate.sh`,\n  `progressive-validate.sh` and `check-completion.sh` already implement it, and\n  each has its own output contract\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add `--quiet`/`-q` parsing, a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, a quiet early return in `output_text()`, and help text |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh` | Create | Regression harness for quiet output, default parity and error paths |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` and `-q` are accepted by the argument parser and set quiet mode without consuming a value. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and text output, stdout contains exactly one line: `Recommended Level: <level> (<name>)`, with no leading blank line, no score line, no breakdown and no phase section. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout and stderr are byte-identical to the pre-change script for every input in the test matrix. |\n| REQ-004 | Exit codes are unchanged: `0` on a successful recommendation, `1` on the existing usage and validation errors. Quiet mode never suppresses a stderr error message. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-005 | `--quiet` composes with the existing flags (`--loc`, `--files`, `--auth`, `--api`, `--db`, `--architectural`, `--recommend-phases`, `--no-recommend-phases`, `--phase-threshold`) in any order, and repeating it is idempotent. |\n| REQ-006 | `--quiet` combined with `--json` leaves the JSON payload unchanged; quiet is a documented no-op in JSON mode so the schema stays single and stable. |\n| REQ-007 | The script header OPTIONS block and `show_help()` both document `--quiet, -q` and the JSON composition rule. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --quiet` prints one line and exits `0`.\n- **SC-002**: A diff of default text output before and after the change is empty across all five matrix inputs.\n- **SC-003**: A diff of `--json` output before and after the change is empty across the same inputs, with and without `--quiet`.\n- **SC-004**: The regression harness passes every row and `bash -n` accepts both the script and the harness.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 compatibility (macOS system bash) | A construct such as `${var,,}` would fail on the default macOS shell | Use the script's existing `[[ \"$VAR\" = true ]]` idiom; no new Bash-4-only syntax |\n| Dependency | `set -euo pipefail` | An unset `QUIET_OUTPUT` aborts the run | Initialize the global beside `JSON_OUTPUT` before parsing; test the no-flag path first |\n| Risk | A quiet branch placed at the wrong layer changes the JSON path too | Breaking change for `speckit-plan.yaml` and `speckit-complete.yaml` callers | Guard inside `output_text()` only; `output_json()` stays untouched and is diff-tested |\n| Risk | Option parsing regresses on a value that looks like a flag | Existing `--loc --quiet` style misuse changes behavior | Keep the existing `[[ \"$2\" =~ ^-- ]]` guards; add matrix rows for missing values |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: The flag adds one boolean branch; total runtime stays within the\n  script's current startup cost and adds no measurable latency for either mode.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The flag accepts no value and opens no new input surface. The\n  script continues to read no environment secrets and writes no files.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for identical inputs. Quiet mode emits the\n  same level and name the default report's first line emits.\n- **NFR-C01**: Default text output and JSON output are backward compatible\n  byte-for-byte; no in-repo caller needs a change.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` alone still fails the existing `At least --loc or --files`\n  validation, exits `1`, and writes the error to stderr only.\n- Maximum length: not applicable; the flag carries no value.\n- Large inputs: `--loc 2000 --files 40 --quiet` still prints one line; phase\n  scoring runs exactly as it does today.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- Missing numeric value after `--loc` or `--files`: unchanged `ERROR:` on stderr\n  and exit `1`, even when `--quiet` is also present.\n- Unknown option: unchanged `ERROR: Unknown option` on stderr and exit `1`.\n- `--quiet` repeated: idempotent, one line.\n- `--quiet --json`: JSON payload unchanged; quiet has no effect in JSON mode.\n- `--quiet --help`: help prints in full and exits `0`; help takes precedence.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 5/25 | Files: 2, LOC: ~40 including the harness, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 5/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N, public CLI surface: Y |\n| Research | 3/20 | Existing option parsing and sibling `--quiet` convention read, no investigation |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **15/100** | **Level 3 declared by the operator for this authoring packet** |\n\nThe change itself scores in Level 0 territory on the script's own algorithm. The\npacket is Level 3 because it was created with `--level 3`; the documentation\ndepth is a deliberate choice, not a complexity signal.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | Default output drifts while adding the quiet branch | H | L | Byte-diff against a captured baseline across five inputs |\n| R-002 | Quiet leaks into the JSON path and breaks command assets | H | L | Guard only in `output_text()`; JSON parity row in the harness |\n| R-003 | A new Bash-4-only construct breaks macOS system bash | M | L | Reuse the existing boolean idiom and run `bash -n` |\n| R-004 | Quiet line drifts from the default report's first line | M | M | Harness asserts equality between the two strings |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line level for automation (Priority: P0)\n\n**As an** automation author wiring `recommend-level.sh` into a hook or prompt\nhelper, **I want** a flag that prints only the level, **so that** I can read one\nvalue without parsing a report whose formatting I do not control.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-001 through AC-007).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Quiet answer for a human operator (Priority: P1)\n\n**As an** operator checking a task's level in a terminal, **I want** a concise\nanswer on demand, **so that** I can see the level without scrolling past a\nbreakdown I did not ask for.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (AC-003, AC-007).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. The quiet-plus-JSON composition is decided in `plan.md` ADR-001, and the\n  flag naming is decided in ADR-002.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: ADR-001 and ADR-002 are recorded in `plan.md` under the\n  L3 Architecture Decision Record section; this packet does not create a separate\n  `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
