{"toolCallId":"call_fb56033c6dfb4f12aa29cb8c778cf725","title":"Ran node","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst p=\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json\";\nconst parsed=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\"));\nconst rules=Array.isArray(parsed)?parsed:(parsed.rules||[]);\nfor(const r of rules) console.log(`${r.rule_id}\\t${r.category}\\t${r.severity}${r.strict_only?\"\\tSTRICT\":\"\"}\\t${r.description}`);\n'","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst p=\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json\";\nconst parsed=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\"));\nconst rules=Array.isArray(parsed)?parsed:(parsed.rules||[]);\nfor(const r of rules) console.log(`${r.rule_id}\\t${r.category}\\t${r.severity}${r.strict_only?\"\\tSTRICT\":\"\"}\\t${r.description}`);\n'","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["node"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_fff1ec823c614c12804671d8baa09375","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add an opt-in quiet output mode to recommend-level.sh by parsing a boolean flag and branching inside the text renderer. The scoring engine, the JSON renderer and every default invocation stay untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet mode implementation\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash (3.2+; the script must run on macOS system bash) |\n| **Framework** | None; standalone CLI script under `runtime/cli/spec/` |\n| **Storage** | None; the script reads no files and writes none |\n| **Testing** | Shell regression harness plus `bash -n` syntax checks |\n\n### Overview\n\nThe change is a single boolean and one branch. The argument parser learns\n`--quiet` and `-q`, a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global joins `JSON_OUTPUT`, and\n`output_text()` returns after printing the recommended-level line when quiet is\nset. `output_json()` is not touched, so the JSON contract and the command assets\nthat consume it stay stable. The harness captures default output before the edit\nand diffs it after, which is the proof that the flag is additive.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Regression harness passes every row\n- [ ] Default and JSON output diffs are empty\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n\nSingle-file CLI with a parse, score, render pipeline. The new flag is an output\nmodifier, not a scoring input, so it belongs to the render stage and must not\nreach the scoring functions.\n\n### Key Components\n\n- **Argument parser** (`§5 MAIN SCRIPT`): the `while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` loop that\n  maps flags to globals. Gains `--quiet|-q`.\n- **Scoring engine** (`calculate_*`, `determine_level`, `determine_phasing`):\n  unchanged. It never reads the quiet flag.\n- **Text renderer** (`output_text()`): owns the human-readable report. Gains the\n  quiet early return.\n- **JSON renderer** (`output_json()`): unchanged. Quiet is a documented no-op\n  here.\n- **Help surface** (file header OPTIONS block and `show_help()`): documents the\n  new flag and the JSON composition rule.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nargv -> parser -> LOC / FILES / risk booleans / JSON_OUTPUT / QUIET_OUTPUT\n                            |\n                            v\n              scoring engine (unchanged)\n                            |\n              +-------------+-------------+\n              v                           v\n     QUIET_OUTPUT = true          QUIET_OUTPUT = false\n     one-line renderer            full text renderer\n              |                           |\n              +-------------+-------------+\n                            v\n                  JSON_OUTPUT = true\n                  (quiet ignored, JSON rendered)\n```\n\nThe quiet branch sits after scoring and before any report formatting, so it\ncannot influence the level, the score or the confidence.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThis packet is an additive feature rather than a bug fix. The inventory below\nrecords every surface the flag touches, so the change cannot drift into a caller\nthat was never considered.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Maps argv to globals | update: accept `--quiet`/`-q` | Matrix rows for flag order, repetition and missing values |\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_text()` | Owns the human-readable report | update: early return under quiet | Quiet row asserts exactly one line |\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_json()` | Owns the JSON payload | unchanged | JSON diff is empty with and without `--quiet` |\n| `recommend-level.sh` header and `show_help()` | Documents options | update: list the flag and JSON rule | `--help` output contains `--quiet` |\n| `speckit-plan.yaml` / `speckit-complete.yaml` | Invoke the script with `--json` | unchanged | They pass no `--quiet`; JSON parity row covers them |\n| `validate.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh` | Already define `--quiet, -q` | unchanged | Convention reference only; no shared code |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level:|output_text|output_json' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`.\n- Consumers of the text report: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled/ --glob '*.sh' --glob '*.yaml' --glob '*.md'`; every in-repo invocation either uses `--json` or is documentation.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, JSON) x quiet (on, off) x input class (valid, invalid) x help.\n- Algorithm invariant: the recommended level is a pure function of the scoring\n  inputs. The quiet flag is not an input to that function, so quiet and default\n  modes must report the same level for the same inputs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Quiet line formatting; default first-line parity | Shell harness with string equality |\n| Integration | Full CLI matrix across text/JSON, flag order and error paths | Shell harness invoking the script as a subprocess |\n| Regression | Byte-diff of default text and JSON output against a captured baseline | `diff` over `scratch/` captures |\n| Manual | `--help` review and a human read of both output modes | Terminal |\n\nThe matrix has five inputs: a minimal task, a medium task with one risk flag, a\nlarge task with three risk flags plus architectural, a phase-heavy task, and a\nJSON-only task. Every input runs in default mode, quiet mode and JSON mode.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; unchanged from today |\n| `diff`, `mktemp`, standard POSIX tools | Internal | Green | Harness cannot compare captures |\n| `shellcheck` (optional) | External | Green | Lint skipped; `bash -n` still gates syntax |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: Default or JSON output diff is non-empty, or an existing caller\n  fails after the change.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh` and\n  delete the harness. The flag is additive, so no caller needs a migration and no\n  data needs repair.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Baseline) ─┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Baseline, Core |\n| Baseline | Setup | Core, Verify |\n| Core | Setup, Baseline | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 0.25-0.5 hours |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 0.5-1 hour |\n| Verification | Low | 0.5-1 hour |\n| **Total** | | **1.25-2.5 hours** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] Backup created (not applicable: no data changes; the baseline captures are the reference)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured (not applicable: `--quiet` is itself the opt-in)\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set (not applicable: local CLI script)\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that changes `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Remove `runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh`.\n3. Re-run the default-output diff against the captured baseline; it must be empty.\n4. Notify no stakeholders: the change has no runtime or user-facing deployment.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 1.5│\n                    │  Baseline │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline captures | None | Default text and JSON snapshots | Core, Verify |\n| Flag parsing | Baseline | `QUIET_OUTPUT` global | Quiet renderer |\n| Quiet renderer | Flag parsing | One-line output | Verify |\n| Help text | Flag parsing | Documented option | Verify |\n| Harness | Quiet renderer, help text | Pass/fail matrix | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the default and JSON baseline** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Parse the flag and add the quiet branch** - 45 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Run the harness and diff the baseline** - 30 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: roughly 1.5 hours\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- The help-text update and the harness can be written alongside the renderer\n  change once the flag name is fixed.\n- The sibling-script convention review can run during baseline capture.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | Default and JSON snapshots stored in `scratch/` | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag implemented | Quiet prints one line; default unchanged | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Verified | Harness green, diffs empty, `bash -n` clean | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet applies to the text renderer only\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The script has two output contracts. `output_text()` serves humans\nand shell callers; `output_json()` serves the `speckit-plan.yaml` and\n`speckit-complete.yaml` command assets. A quiet flag could either filter both or\nfilter only the human report.\n\n**Decision**: `--quiet` branches inside `output_text()` and is a documented no-op\nwith `--json`. The JSON schema stays single, and JSON callers keep the payload\nthey already parse.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: no JSON schema fork, no consumer changes, one obvious place to read\n  the quiet behavior.\n- Negative: a JSON caller cannot ask for a reduced payload. Mitigation: the\n  payload already carries `recommended_level` as its first field, so a consumer\n  that wants one value can select it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Quiet filters both renderers: it would either change the JSON schema or emit a\n  second, quiet-only JSON shape, both of which break the existing contract.\n- Quiet plus JSON is a usage error: it turns a harmless combination into a\n  failure and adds a validation branch for no benefit.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: Follow the sibling `--quiet, -q` convention\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `validate.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `check-completion.sh`\nalready expose `--quiet` with the `-q` alias. The new flag could use a different\nname, such as `--level-only`, or match the convention.\n\n**Decision**: Use `--quiet` and `-q`, matching the sibling scripts.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one vocabulary across the spec CLI; users transfer the flag without\n  reading help.\n- Negative: `--quiet` in the siblings means \"minimal output\", while here it means\n  \"one line\". Mitigation: the help text states the exact line that is printed.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- `--level-only`: more precise, but it adds a second quiet vocabulary to the same\n  CLI family.\n- `--porcelain`: conventional for stable machine output, but it implies a\n  format guarantee this change does not need.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: Guard inside `output_text()` rather than at the dispatch site\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The quiet branch could live in the `§7 OUTPUT RESULTS` dispatch or\ninside `output_text()`.\n\n**Decision**: Put the early return at the top of `output_text()`. The dispatch\nstays a two-way choice between the renderers, and the quiet behavior lives with\nthe report it suppresses.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one function owns all text-output decisions; the dispatch remains\n  unchanged.\n- Negative: `output_text()` grows by one branch. Mitigation: the branch is three\n  lines and returns immediately.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A third `output_quiet()` renderer: it duplicates the format string, which then\n  has two homes and can drift from the report's first line.\n- Dispatch-site guard: it splits knowledge of the report format across two\n  functions.\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add an opt-in quiet output mode to recommend-level.sh by parsing a boolean flag and branching inside the text renderer. The scoring engine, the JSON renderer and every default invocation stay untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet mode implementation\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.2 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash (3.2+; the script must run on macOS system bash) |\n| **Framework** | None; standalone CLI script under `runtime/cli/spec/` |\n| **Storage** | None; the script reads no files and writes none |\n| **Testing** | Shell regression harness plus `bash -n` syntax checks |\n\n### Overview\n\nThe change is a single boolean and one branch. The argument parser learns\n`--quiet` and `-q`, a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global joins `JSON_OUTPUT`, and\n`output_text()` returns after printing the recommended-level line when quiet is\nset. `output_json()` is not touched, so the JSON contract and the command assets\nthat consume it stay stable. The harness captures default output before the edit\nand diffs it after, which is the proof that the flag is additive.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Regression harness passes every row\n- [ ] Default and JSON output diffs are empty\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n\nSingle-file CLI with a parse, score, render pipeline. The new flag is an output\nmodifier, not a scoring input, so it belongs to the render stage and must not\nreach the scoring functions.\n\n### Key Components\n\n- **Argument parser** (`§5 MAIN SCRIPT`): the `while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` loop that\n  maps flags to globals. Gains `--quiet|-q`.\n- **Scoring engine** (`calculate_*`, `determine_level`, `determine_phasing`):\n  unchanged. It never reads the quiet flag.\n- **Text renderer** (`output_text()`): owns the human-readable report. Gains the\n  quiet early return.\n- **JSON renderer** (`output_json()`): unchanged. Quiet is a documented no-op\n  here.\n- **Help surface** (file header OPTIONS block and `show_help()`): documents the\n  new flag and the JSON composition rule.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nargv -> parser -> LOC / FILES / risk booleans / JSON_OUTPUT / QUIET_OUTPUT\n                            |\n                            v\n              scoring engine (unchanged)\n                            |\n              +-------------+-------------+\n              v                           v\n     QUIET_OUTPUT = true          QUIET_OUTPUT = false\n     one-line renderer            full text renderer\n              |                           |\n              +-------------+-------------+\n                            v\n                  JSON_OUTPUT = true\n                  (quiet ignored, JSON rendered)\n```\n\nThe quiet branch sits after scoring and before any report formatting, so it\ncannot influence the level, the score or the confidence.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThis packet is an additive feature rather than a bug fix. The inventory below\nrecords every surface the flag touches, so the change cannot drift into a caller\nthat was never considered.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Maps argv to globals | update: accept `--quiet`/`-q` | Matrix rows for flag order, repetition and missing values |\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_text()` | Owns the human-readable report | update: early return under quiet | Quiet row asserts exactly one line |\n| `recommend-level.sh` `output_json()` | Owns the JSON payload | unchanged | JSON diff is empty with and without `--quiet` |\n| `recommend-level.sh` header and `show_help()` | Documents options | update: list the flag and JSON rule | `--help` output contains `--quiet` |\n| `speckit-plan.yaml` / `speckit-complete.yaml` | Invoke the script with `--json` | unchanged | They pass no `--quiet`; JSON parity row covers them |\n| `validate.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh` | Already define `--quiet, -q` | unchanged | Convention reference only; no shared code |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level:|output_text|output_json' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`.\n- Consumers of the text report: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled/ --glob '*.sh' --glob '*.yaml' --glob '*.md'`; every in-repo invocation either uses `--json` or is documentation.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, JSON) x quiet (on, off) x input class (valid, invalid) x help.\n- Algorithm invariant: the recommended level is a pure function of the scoring\n  inputs. The quiet flag is not an input to that function, so quiet and default\n  modes must report the same level for the same inputs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Quiet line formatting; default first-line parity | Shell harness with string equality |\n| Integration | Full CLI matrix across text/JSON, flag order and error paths | Shell harness invoking the script as a subprocess |\n| Regression | Byte-diff of default text and JSON output against a captured baseline | `diff` over `scratch/` captures |\n| Manual | `--help` review and a human read of both output modes | Terminal |\n\nThe matrix has five inputs: a minimal task, a medium task with one risk flag, a\nlarge task with three risk flags plus architectural, a phase-heavy task, and a\nJSON-only task. Every input runs in default mode, quiet mode and JSON mode.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; unchanged from today |\n| `diff`, `mktemp`, standard POSIX tools | Internal | Green | Harness cannot compare captures |\n| `shellcheck` (optional) | External | Green | Lint skipped; `bash -n` still gates syntax |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: Default or JSON output diff is non-empty, or an existing caller\n  fails after the change.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh` and\n  delete the harness. The flag is additive, so no caller needs a migration and no\n  data needs repair.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Baseline) ─┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Baseline, Core |\n| Baseline | Setup | Core, Verify |\n| Core | Setup, Baseline | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 0.25-0.5 hours |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 0.5-1 hour |\n| Verification | Low | 0.5-1 hour |\n| **Total** | | **1.25-2.5 hours** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] Backup created (not applicable: no data changes; the baseline captures are the reference)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured (not applicable: `--quiet` is itself the opt-in)\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set (not applicable: local CLI script)\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that changes `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Remove `runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet-flag.sh`.\n3. Re-run the default-output diff against the captured baseline; it must be empty.\n4. Notify no stakeholders: the change has no runtime or user-facing deployment.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 1.5│\n                    │  Baseline │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline captures | None | Default text and JSON snapshots | Core, Verify |\n| Flag parsing | Baseline | `QUIET_OUTPUT` global | Quiet renderer |\n| Quiet renderer | Flag parsing | One-line output | Verify |\n| Help text | Flag parsing | Documented option | Verify |\n| Harness | Quiet renderer, help text | Pass/fail matrix | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the default and JSON baseline** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Parse the flag and add the quiet branch** - 45 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Run the harness and diff the baseline** - 30 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: roughly 1.5 hours\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- The help-text update and the harness can be written alongside the renderer\n  change once the flag name is fixed.\n- The sibling-script convention review can run during baseline capture.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | Default and JSON snapshots stored in `scratch/` | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag implemented | Quiet prints one line; default unchanged | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Verified | Harness green, diffs empty, `bash -n` clean | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nBefore starting any task from `tasks.md`, confirm:\n\n1. The task id and its file path are the ones named in `tasks.md`; a mismatch\n   stops the run.\n2. The baseline captures from T002 exist and are readable.\n3. The working tree carries no unrelated modification to `recommend-level.sh`.\n4. The acceptance criterion the task serves is known.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Execute tasks in id order. T004 through T008 touch one file and must not be reordered across a verification run. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only the files a task names. `output_json()` and the scoring functions are read-only surfaces for this packet. |\n| TASK-EVIDENCE | A task is complete only when its command output and exit status have been read, not when the edit applied. |\n| TASK-HALT | Stop and report on a failed edit anchor, a non-empty output diff, or a failing harness row. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nReport each task as `T### <state> - <evidence>`, where state is `done`, `blocked`\nor `skipped`, and evidence is the command plus its result. Example:\n`T011 done - harness 14/14 rows pass`.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nMark the task `[B]` in `tasks.md` and record the blocker, what was tried and the\nsmallest next action. A blocked P0 task stops the packet; a blocked P1 task needs\noperator approval before it can be deferred.\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet applies to the text renderer only\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The script has two output contracts. `output_text()` serves humans\nand shell callers; `output_json()` serves the `speckit-plan.yaml` and\n`speckit-complete.yaml` command assets. A quiet flag could either filter both or\nfilter only the human report.\n\n**Decision**: `--quiet` branches inside `output_text()` and is a documented no-op\nwith `--json`. The JSON schema stays single, and JSON callers keep the payload\nthey already parse.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: no JSON schema fork, no consumer changes, one obvious place to read\n  the quiet behavior.\n- Negative: a JSON caller cannot ask for a reduced payload. Mitigation: the\n  payload already carries `recommended_level` as its first field, so a consumer\n  that wants one value can select it.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Quiet filters both renderers: it would either change the JSON schema or emit a\n  second, quiet-only JSON shape, both of which break the existing contract.\n- Quiet plus JSON is a usage error: it turns a harmless combination into a\n  failure and adds a validation branch for no benefit.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: Follow the sibling `--quiet, -q` convention\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `validate.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh` and `check-completion.sh`\nalready expose `--quiet` with the `-q` alias. The new flag could use a different\nname, such as `--level-only`, or match the convention.\n\n**Decision**: Use `--quiet` and `-q`, matching the sibling scripts.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one vocabulary across the spec CLI; users transfer the flag without\n  reading help.\n- Negative: `--quiet` in the siblings means \"minimal output\", while here it means\n  \"one line\". Mitigation: the help text states the exact line that is printed.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- `--level-only`: more precise, but it adds a second quiet vocabulary to the same\n  CLI family.\n- `--porcelain`: conventional for stable machine output, but it implies a\n  format guarantee this change does not need.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: Guard inside `output_text()` rather than at the dispatch site\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The quiet branch could live in the `§7 OUTPUT RESULTS` dispatch or\ninside `output_text()`.\n\n**Decision**: Put the early return at the top of `output_text()`. The dispatch\nstays a two-way choice between the renderers, and the quiet behavior lives with\nthe report it suppresses.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Positive: one function owns all text-output decisions; the dispatch remains\n  unchanged.\n- Negative: `output_text()` grows by one branch. Mitigation: the branch is three\n  lines and returns immediately.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A third `output_quiet()` renderer: it duplicates the format string, which then\n  has two homes and can drift from the report's first line.\n- Dispatch-site guard: it splits knowledge of the report format across two\n  functions.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":35,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/222-deepseek-baseline/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
